The deltas shown by GitHub may be a little hard to follow, but if you look at the revised code I think that you will see that using controlflow.TryFinally makes it easier to follow (making the order of the source agree with the order of execution).

I could have used TryFinally in more or fewer cases. I chose to use it to replace the pattern below.

```go
func() {
    defer func() {
        ... some code that certainly runs, later...
    }()
    ... some code that runs earlier ...
}()
```

